### Lab 10: CommentService.delete, GlobalApiExceptionHandler and the AOP log.
### Run the requests one after another: 1-3 sign in as ADMIN (session cookie + CSRF token).

### 1. Login page: take the CSRF token
GET http://localhost:8088/login

> {%
  client.global.set("csrf", response.body.match(/name="_csrf" value="([^"]+)"/)[1]);
%}

### 2. Sign in as ADMIN (the cookie jar keeps JSESSIONID)
POST http://localhost:8088/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

email=admin@bookshelf.test&password=admin123&_csrf={{csrf}}

### 3. Comments of book 1: new CSRF token after login, the oldest seed comment
GET http://localhost:8088/comments?bookId=1

> {%
  const html = response.body;
  client.global.set("csrf", html.match(/name="_csrf" value="([^"]+)"/)[1]);
  const forms = [...html.matchAll(/name="commentId" value="(\d+)">\s*<input type="hidden" name="createdAt" value="([^"]+)"/g)];
  const last = forms[forms.length - 1];
  client.global.set("oldId", last[1]);
  client.global.set("oldCreatedAt", last[2]);
  client.log("Oldest comment: id=" + last[1] + ", createdAt=" + last[2]);
%}

### 4. Invalid bookId -> 400 + JSON {"error": "..."}
POST http://localhost:8088/comments/delete
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Accept: application/json

bookId=0&commentId=1&createdAt={{$isoTimestamp}}&_csrf={{csrf}}

### 5. Missing createdAt -> 400 + JSON
POST http://localhost:8088/comments/delete
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Accept: application/json

bookId=1&commentId=1&_csrf={{csrf}}

### 6. Seed comment older than 24 hours -> 400 + JSON
POST http://localhost:8088/comments/delete
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Accept: application/json

bookId=1&commentId={{oldId}}&createdAt={{oldCreatedAt}}&_csrf={{csrf}}

### 7. Forged createdAt for the same old comment -> 400 + JSON (the stored time wins)
POST http://localhost:8088/comments/delete
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Accept: application/json

bookId=1&commentId={{oldId}}&createdAt={{$isoTimestamp}}&_csrf={{csrf}}

### 8. Book that does not exist -> 404 + JSON
POST http://localhost:8088/comments/delete
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Accept: application/json

bookId=999999&commentId=1&createdAt={{$isoTimestamp}}&_csrf={{csrf}}

### 9. Add a fresh comment as ADMIN
# @no-redirect
POST http://localhost:8088/comments?bookId=1
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

text=Свіжий коментар для перевірки видалення (лаба 10)&_csrf={{csrf}}

### 10. Newest comment of book 1 (sorted by createdAt desc)
GET http://localhost:8088/comments?bookId=1

> {%
  const first = response.body.match(/name="commentId" value="(\d+)">\s*<input type="hidden" name="createdAt" value="([^"]+)"/);
  client.global.set("newId", first[1]);
  client.global.set("newCreatedAt", first[2]);
  client.log("Newest comment: id=" + first[1] + ", createdAt=" + first[2]);
%}

### 11. Valid delete -> 302 to /comments?bookId=1, see the AOP log in the AppInit console
# @no-redirect
POST http://localhost:8088/comments/delete
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

bookId=1&commentId={{newId}}&createdAt={{newCreatedAt}}&_csrf={{csrf}}
